    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11843" root="خيط" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِيَاطٌ</span></b>  <i>A needle;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِخْيَطٌ</span></b> . (S, Msb, * K.)
Hence the saying in the Kur [vii. 38], <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَتَّى يَلِجَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَبَلُ فِى سَمِّ الخِيَاطِ</span> [<i>Until the camel enter into
the eye of the needle</i>]. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَيْطٌ</span>, in
three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخِيطٌ</span>.

